1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,734
Let me be honest with you about the timeline.

2
00:00:02,734 --> 00:00:05,816
Under the scheme, plants get two years to be built.

3
00:00:05,816 --> 00:00:07,910
Then five years of support.

4
00:00:07,910 --> 00:00:11,604
And China has a head start of more than thirty years.

5
00:00:11,604 --> 00:00:16,178
Running hundreds of tanks well, every single day, takes practice.

6
00:00:16,178 --> 00:00:17,921
You can't buy that overnight.

7
00:00:17,921 --> 00:00:20,350
So here's the rule I take from all this.

8
00:00:20,350 --> 00:00:24,841
If you only sell the sand, you sell cheap and you buy expensive.

9
00:00:24,841 --> 00:00:26,102
And the price of that?

10
00:00:26,102 --> 00:00:29,664
When the one seller says stop, your factories stop.

11
00:00:29,664 --> 00:00:31,074
You saw it in Pune.

12
00:00:31,074 --> 00:00:32,992
But here's the reality today.

13
00:00:32,992 --> 00:00:34,528
India has the sand.

14
00:00:34,528 --> 00:00:35,980
It has the scientists.

15
00:00:35,980 --> 00:00:37,934
And now it has the money.

16
00:00:37,934 --> 00:00:42,550
What's left is the hard middle — more tanks, and the furnaces.

17
00:00:42,550 --> 00:00:44,372
So what does this mean for you?

18
00:00:44,372 --> 00:00:48,606
If you're planning to buy an electric scooter or a new phone, remember this.

19
00:00:48,606 --> 00:00:56,484
A small magnet inside it depends on this chain — and that can change its price, and even when it reaches your showroom.

20
00:00:56,484 --> 00:00:57,793
Watch two things.

21
00:00:57,793 --> 00:01:01,678
November tenth — does China's pause end, or get stretched?

22
00:01:01,678 --> 00:01:06,993
And the scheme winners — the five companies that will try to build India's own magnets.

23
00:01:06,993 --> 00:01:09,174
India won't fix this in one jump.

24
00:01:09,174 --> 00:01:12,401
It'll be tank by tank... furnace by furnace.

25
00:01:12,401 --> 00:01:15,067
And magnets aren't the only missing piece.

26
00:01:15,067 --> 00:01:21,714
India is called the pharmacy of the world... but a big share of the ingredients in your medicines comes from China.

27
00:01:21,714 --> 00:01:22,530
Why?

28
00:01:22,530 --> 00:01:24,080
That's our next story.

29
00:01:24,080 --> 00:01:26,382
Which missing piece should we open after that?

30
00:01:26,382 --> 00:01:27,417
Tell me in the comments.

31
00:01:27,417 --> 00:01:28,903
I read every one.

32
00:01:28,903 --> 00:01:30,781
This is Be Practical with Kishore.

33
00:01:30,781 --> 00:01:31,879
Stay practical.

34
00:01:31,879 --> 00:01:32,526
Jai Hind.

